its own\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"EST-25\",\n   \"title\": \"Project management: client liaison\",\n   \"feature\": \"F-1\",\n   \"track\": \"pm\",\n   \"kind\": \"pm-management\",\n   \"executor\": \"human\",\n   \"complexity\": \"standard\",\n   \"items\": [],\n   \"dependsOn\": [],\n   \"overhead\": \"Client calls, scope decisions and sign-offs\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"EST-26\",\n   \"title\": \"Handover notes\",\n   \"feature\": \"F-1\",\n   \"track\": \"pdm\",\n   \"kind\": \"pdm-docs\",\n   \"executor\": \"factory\",\n   \"complexity\": \"standard\",\n   \"items\": [\n    \"How staff update order status directly in the database (ASM-6)\",\n    \"Deployment and configuration notes\"\n   ],\n   \"dependsOn\": [],\n   \"overhead\": \"Documentation delivers no requirement on its own\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"requirements\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n  \"ears\": \"The portal shall provide exactly three screens for the signed-in buyer: Find parts at /parts, Cart and checkout at /cart, and My orders at /orders with the order detail panel on the same page.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a buyer requests the parts list, the parts API shall return parts sorted by name A–Z, 20 per page, each with image (or none), name, part number, brand, price in GBP with 2 decimals, stock state and stock quantity as a whole number.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"ears\": \"The parts API shall set a part's stock state to \\\"In stock\\\" when stock is 5 or more, \\\"Low stock (n left)\\\" when stock is 1 to 4, and \\\"Out of stock\\\" when stock is 0.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the search text has at least 2 characters, the parts API shall return only parts whose name or part number contains that text, ignoring letter case.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the buyer picks a category or brand filter, the parts API shall return only parts matching that one category and that one brand, combined with any search text, where \\\"All\\\" means no filter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the search text or a filter changes on Find parts, the portal shall show page 1 of the results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"ears\": \"When no part matches the search and filters, the portal shall show \\\"No parts match\\\" and a button that clears the search and filters.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the buyer presses \\\"Add to cart\\\" on a part that is in stock, the cart shall add a line with quantity 1, or raise the existing line's quantity by 1.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"ears\": \"The portal shall show in the header a cart count equal to the total of all quantities in the cart, updated whenever the cart changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"ears\": \"If a part is out of stock, then the portal shall disable its \\\"Add to cart\\\" button.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"ears\": \"The cart shall give each line its name, part number, unit price, quantity and line total, where line total = unit price × quantity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the buyer changes a line quantity, the cart shall recalculate that line total and the order totals at once.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n  \"ears\": \"If the buyer enters a quantity that is blank, 0, above 99 or not a whole number, then the cart shall set it to the nearest whole number from 1 to 99.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n  \"ears\": \"If the buyer enters a quantity above the part's stock, then the cart shall set the quantity to the stock quantity and give the message \\\"Only n available\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the buyer presses \\\"Remove\\\" on a cart line, the cart shall remove that line.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n  \"ears\": \"The cart shall keep its lines in the browser's local storage under the signed-in buyer's ID, so the cart survives page reloads on the same device.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n  \"ears\": \"While the cart is empty, the portal shall show \\\"Your cart is empty\\\" with a link to Find parts and hide checkout.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n  \"ears\": \"The checkout shall enable \\\"Place order\\\" only when the delivery address has 5 to 200 characters and a delivery option (Standard or Next day) is selected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n  \"ears\": \"The checkout shall show subtotal, delivery charge (Standard £0.00, Next day £9.99) and total, where total = subtotal + delivery charge.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the buyer places an order with valid lines, address and delivery option, the orders API shall save an order with status Placed, a sequential order number ORD- followed by 6 zero-padded digits, each line's current part price as unit price, and total = subtotal + delivery charge.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-21\",\n  \"ears\": \"If a place-order request has no lines, a quantity outside 1–99, an unknown part number, an address outside 5–200 characters, or a missing or unknown delivery option, then the orders API shall reject it with status 400 and save no order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-22\",\n  \"ears\": \"If any line's quantity is above the part's stock when an order is placed, then the orders API shall reject the order with status 409 and return each affected part number with the stock now available, saving no order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-23\",\n  \"ears\": \"When an order is placed successfully, the portal shall empty the cart and show the new order number.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-24\",\n  \"ears\": \"If placing an order fails with a network error or a server error, then the portal shall show an error message, which for a network error tells the buyer to check My orders before retrying, and keep the cart lines, address and delivery option so the buyer can try again.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-25\",\n  \"ears\": \"The orders API shall leave the stock quantity in the parts database unchanged when an order is placed or cancelled.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-27\",\n  \"ears\": \"The orders API shall return to a buyer only the orders placed by that buyer.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-28\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a buyer requests their orders, the orders API shall return them newest first, each with order number, date placed, number of items (total of all quantities), total and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-29\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the buyer picks a status filter on My orders, the orders API shall return only that buyer's orders with that status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-30\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a buyer opens one of their orders, the orders API shall return its lines (part number, name, quantity, unit price), delivery address, delivery option, total and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-31\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the buyer opens an order, the portal shall show a status timeline Placed → Packed → Dispatched → Delivered with the current status marked by text as well as colour.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-32\",\n  \"ears\": \"While an order's status is Placed, the portal shall show a \\\"Cancel order\\\" button in the order detail that asks for confirmation before calling the cancel API.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-33\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a buyer cancels their order whose status is still Placed, the orders API shall set the status to Cancelled.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-34\",\n  \"ears\": \"If the order's status is no longer Placed when the buyer confirms cancelling, then the orders API shall refuse with status 409 and leave the status unchanged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-35\",\n  \"ears\": \"While the buyer has no orders, the portal shall show \\\"No orders yet\\\" and a link to Find parts on My orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-36\",\n  \"ears\": \"The portal shall show all three screens without horizontal scrolling at viewport widths from 360 px upwards.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-37\",\n  \"ears\": \"The portal shall give every form field a visible text label and let the buyer reach and use every control by keyboard alone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-38\",\n  \"ears\": \"While the parts database holds 5,000 parts, the Find parts screen shall load its first page of results in under 2 seconds.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-39\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the orders API rejects an order with a 409 stock conflict, the cart shall lower each affected line to the stock now available with the message \\\"Only n available\\\", remove each affected line whose available stock is 0 with the message \\\"<part name> is now out of stock\\\", and keep all other lines.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-40\",\n  \"ears\": \"While a place-order request is in progress, the checkout shall disable \\\"Place order\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-41\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the buyer opens the cart, the cart shall fetch the current price of each line's part from the parts API and use only those current prices for unit prices, line totals and totals.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-42\",\n  \"ears\": \"If the current part data fetched when the cart opens shows a cart line's part has 0 stock, then the cart shall remove that line and give the message \\\"<part name> is now out of stock\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-43\",\n  \"ears\": \"If the request to the parts API for current prices fails with a network or server error when the cart opens, then the cart shall show the cart lines without unit prices, line totals or totals, show an error message with a \\\"Try again\\\" button, and hide checkout until current prices load.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"settings\" kind=\"settings\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"deliveryModel\": \"agentic\",\n \"stackSource\": \"client\",\n \"designInTotal\": true,\n \"feedbackRounds\": 2,\n \"noRepo\": true,\n \"client\": \"Demo Garage\",\n \"projectName\": \"Parts Quick Order\",\n \"humanReview\": true\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"known-stack\" kind=\"known-stack\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"repo\": false,\n \"stackChosenBy\": \"client\"\n}\n</artifact>\n\nSize the tasks (independent estimator 2 of 3)."}